\ by-constructor when two constructors apply: the first, Or.inl, as Lean
\ chooses (Lean also warns that Or.inr matches; LeanForth prints no
\ warnings) (slice a2-iii; tests/front/tactics/goal-layer.lean). The
\ term is Or.inl h.
\ Lean: theorem co_or (a : Nat) (h : a ≤ a) : a ≤ a ∨ a ≤ a + 1 := by
\         constructor
\         exact h
theorem co_or
  Nat explicit: a
  a a ≤ explicit: h
  a a ≤ a a 1 + ≤ Or
:= by
  by-constructor
  ' h by-exact
end co_or
